---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const example = `- uses: beastrog/aethens@v0.1.0
  with:
    path: path/to/tasks
    budget: standard
    fail-on: error
    seed: "0"`;
---

<Docs
  current="action"
  title="GitHub Action"
  description="Inputs, outputs, and example workflow YAML for the Aethens GitHub Action, pinned to beastrog/aethens@v0.1.0."
>
  <p class="kicker mb-5"><span>Docs</span><span class="num" aria-hidden="true">/</span><span>Action</span></p>
  <h1 class="font-serif italic font-semibold text-section leading-[1.1]">GitHub Action</h1>
  <p class="mt-6 text-paper/90">
    The composite Action in this repository runs the verifiers of code tasks
    against the gold solution, labelled candidates, and mutants, and reports
    problems with evidence and repro commands. Use it on
    <code class="text-gold">pull_request</code> with read-only permissions. It
    needs no secrets.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    The example pins <code class="text-gold">beastrog/aethens@v0.1.0</code>, the
    current release, also listed on the{' '}
    <a class="prose-link" href="https://github.com/marketplace/actions/aethens-audit">GitHub Marketplace</a>.
    The Action installs Aethens from its own checkout, so the ref you pin is the
    version that runs. The <code class="text-gold">path</code> input is relative
    to the workspace, so the job must check out your repository first.
  </p>

  <h2 id="example" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Example</h2>
  <pre class="cmd mt-4" tabindex="0"><code>{example}</code></pre>
  <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-muted">
    Same example as the README. Optional inputs
    <code class="text-gold">images</code> and
    <code class="text-gold">python-version</code> can be added as needed.
  </p>

  <h2 id="inputs" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Inputs</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-paper/90">
    From <code class="text-gold">action.yml</code>:
  </p>
  <div class="scroll-x mt-6">
    <table class="sheet">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Input</th>
          <th>Required</th>
          <th>Default</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>path</code></td>
          <td>yes</td>
          <td>—</td>
          <td>Task directory (with <code>task.yaml</code>) or a directory of tasks, relative to the workspace.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>budget</code></td>
          <td>no</td>
          <td><code>standard</code></td>
          <td><code>smoke</code>, <code>standard</code>, or <code>deep</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>fail-on</code></td>
          <td>no</td>
          <td><code>error</code></td>
          <td><code>error</code> or <code>warning</code>. Findings at or above this severity fail the step.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>seed</code></td>
          <td>no</td>
          <td><code>0</code></td>
          <td>Seed for reproducible runs.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>images</code></td>
          <td>no</td>
          <td><code>python:3.12-slim</code></td>
          <td>Space-separated Docker images the tasks use. The Action pulls them before the audit; runs use <code>--pull never</code>.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>python-version</code></td>
          <td>no</td>
          <td><code>3.12</code></td>
          <td>Python used to run Aethens itself, not the tasks, which run in Docker.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="outputs" class="mt-12 font-serif italic text-2xl">Outputs</h2>
  <div class="scroll-x mt-6">
    <table class="sheet">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Output</th>
          <th>Description</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>exit-code</code></td>
          <td>The aethens exit code: 0 pass, 1 findings, 2 tool error, 3 timeout.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p class="mt-6 text-paper/90">
    The Action always runs <code class="text-gold">aethens audit</code> with
    <code class="text-gold">--format markdown</code> and
    <code class="text-gold">--output aethens-report.md</code>. If that report file
    exists, it is appended to the GitHub Actions step summary. The step then
    exits with the same code Aethens returned, so findings at or above
    <code class="text-gold">fail-on</code> fail the job.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-8 text-sm text-muted">
    Sources: <code>action.yml</code>, the README Action example, and
    <code>.github/workflows/action-selftest.yml</code> (read-only
    <code>pull_request</code> usage).
    CLI flags: <a class="prose-link" href={`${base}docs/cli/`}>CLI usage</a>.
  </p>
</Docs>
